{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '401,520p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"**§7.11** (`:2931-2942`): rename \"Continuation conformance harness\"; \"to each safepoint of the complete §7.4.1 table — effect-producing calls included —\" → \"to **every boundary of the stepping driver** (continuation design §5.7), the complete §7.4.1 table's parking transitions included,\"; the cross-engine sentence \"one program at one aligned instruction boundary\". **§7.11.1** (`:3100-3130`): Invariant → \"At every instruction boundary, lifting and lowering preserve the next observable step (and, at a parking transition, its wait; with a non-empty queue, its order); a pc outside every body refuses.\" Setup: \"a nonsafepoint pc\" → \"a `:push` pc of the stack image (relabels) and a body-start pc (lifts)\"; expected: \"An undeclared pc gives `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; queued work gives `:yin.k/not-quiescent`\" → \"A pc outside every body gives `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; every pc of A lifts as a `run` state when the machine is between instructions; queued work travels as `:ready` rows and resumes in order\".\n\n#### 3.7.4 `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`\n\n**§1 stance item 1** (`:45-49`): append \"Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc): a *safepoint* is a parking `(segment-address, pc)`; the carrier expresses every `(segment-address, pc)` of A as a `:run` state when the machine is between instructions, and the scheduler's completed wakes as `:ready` rows.\" **§5.2**: `:run` and `:ready` rows; `:wait`'s note. **§5.5** (`:455-460`): the kind-rules paragraph = plan v2 §3.1 table; keep \"Frames restore in carried order and are never collapsed to one; a task may hold several ordered waits **and several ordered completed wakes**\". Custody table (`:466-473`): rows `root | running / blocked / parked | exclusive | the four keys plus origin on a successor` and `root | running / blocked / parked | fork | nil`; add \"a completed `:put` wake is a completed operation: its op-id is well-formed, not retained\". **§8 step 7** (`:797-801`): contexts \"(`:wait`, `:captured`, `:parked`, `:running`)\" and \"the root's `:run` and each `:ready`'s wait\". **§9 Lift** (`:880`): \"the merged order is holds, kind, free environment …\" (quiescence deleted); the canonical round-trip law (`:913-917`) unchanged (\"no execution between lower and lift\" is the law the harness now follows literally); **Cross-engine** (`:929`): \"Running the corpus to each aligned instruction boundary\". **§11** (`:1027`): \"Code identity (A), the parking transitions,\".\n\n#### 3.7.5 `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md` §7 (`:560-579`)\n\nReplace \"Only blocked, explicitly parked or halted tasks at the existing engine export boundary are eligible. Running CESK/PC snapshots are not a fourth kind.\" with:\n\n> **Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc).** For the stack-shaped machine of versions 0-2, only blocked, explicitly parked or halted tasks were eligible and running snapshots were not a fourth kind. For the register-shaped machine and body version 3 this is reversed by the owner's invariant: a task between instructions is the fourth kind, `:running`, carried with its ordered waits and completed wakes (continuation design §1.3, §2.6), and is eligible for export and custody.\n\n#### 3.7.6 `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` §14.1\n\nTable 14.1.1 (`:3777-3788`): add `| Between instructions (:running) | Active control; ordered waits and completed wakes travel; the window is exactly L(pc); continue at pc. |`. `:3798` \"Static `:yin.safepoint/kinds` checks pc eligibility only\" → \"…checks a parking pc's kinds; a `run` pc is any pc of a body\". `:3827` → \"Validate the instruction boundary (§7.4.1 as amended); enter exporting before …\". `:3882` \"continue to the next safepoint\" → \"continue to the next park, halt or fuel boundary\". `:3900-3901` → \"A pc outside every body yields `not-at-safepoint`; queued work travels as `:ready` rows.\" `:4145` as UCF §7.8 step 9.\n\n#### 3.7.7 `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`\n\nNew dated entry I-9: \"2026-10-16, any-pc. The lift refuses a machine between instructions (`rows.cljc:1656-1657`) and a non-empty ready queue (`:1652-1653`), the holder runs to a park (`driver.cljc:2120`), and every custody kind table lists three kinds, in violation of the owner's primary invariant (2026-10-17). Slices 6d-a, 6d-b and 6e add the `:run` and `:ready` rows, root kind `:running`, validator rules R1-R2 and the extended S1/C2/C3/P1, custody for running roots, fuel, expiry semantics, control-flow stack layouts and the harness at every boundary. Section 8's 'check the pc against the static safepoint set' (`:602`) and 'the safepoint harness must run each 7.4.1 row' (`:622`) describe the stack-shaped machine and are historical.\" No compatibility promise.\n\n#### 3.7.8 The assessment's §F and the gap list\n\nAssessment §F disagreement 3 → \"Safepoints are the parking transitions, a proper subset of the representable boundaries, by the owner's invariant; its 'one necessity kept' (the ready-queue refusal) was wrong: the queue is carried.\" Its verdict line is superseded by this report. Gap list G7 (\"capability gap only\") superseded; the orchestrator log's next seat entry records the reclassification as a P1 defect against a primary invariant and cites this report. `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` gains the row:\n\n> | the lift refuses a machine between instructions (`rows.cljc:1656-1657`) and a queued completed wake (`:1652-1653`), the holder runs to a park (`driver.cljc:2120`) and loses a computed boundary on tenure loss (`:2252-2253`), the custody kind tables list three kinds, and the stack layout is undefined at jump pcs (`layout.cljc:118-131`): the carrier cannot express, and the holder cannot pause at, an arbitrary pc | owner invariant 2026-10-17; Architect plan v2 `collab/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md` | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | 6d-a, 6d-b, 6e | P1 |\n\n### 3.8 Complete inventory of safepoint-only assertions\n\nMethod: `grep -rn safepoint docs/ src/ test/` on `7c4dff32`, every hit classified. **Excluded as a different concept**: guest-visible event-delivery safepoints (`yang.safepoint`, `yang.stage`, `yang.python.antlr.safepoint`/`lower`/`prelude`, their tests `test/yang/**`, `test/yin/vm/semantic/scan_test.cljc:15,30`, `derive_test.cljc:9,637`, `stream_poll_test.cljc:2`, `docs/design/yang.antlr.md` (48 hits), `yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md:653,985,989`, `test.subsystems.md:78`, `src/dev/subsystems.edn:55`, `build-n-test.md:44`): delivery at an arbitrary pc would be implicit control flow visible to the guest; migration at an arbitrary pc is invisible. One footnote at `yang.antlr.md:1340-1341` makes the distinction. **Historical logs** (`docs/orchestrator-log.md`, 103 hits; `docs/cesk-space-optimization.md:85,117`): append-only; the next seat entry records supersession; no rewrite. **The driver's `:safepoint` phase name** (`driver.cljc:74,100,1122,1130,1796,2041,2147-2179,2309,2359`; `driver_test.cljc` 20 hits; `compose_test.cljc:509-551`; `compose_rows_test.cljc` 19 hits; `stage_e_scenarios.cljc` `[:until \"h1\" :safepoint n]` 14 hits): the phase means \"the machine has nothing left to drive, or the exit is armed\"; keep the name, fix the docstring at `:74-77` (\"halted, no wait, or the composition armed the exit over a machine at a park or an instruction boundary\"), and `at-safepoint?` (`:2147-2154`) keeps detecting the halt with a docstring saying so.\n\n**Rule statements to replace** (the sentence says \"only at a safepoint\" or an equivalent):\n\n| File:line | Text | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `universal-continuation-format.md:17` | \"The safepoint set must be exactly the machine's parking transitions\" | §3.7.3 |\n| `:127`, `:151` | \"the safepoints of §4.1\"; \"the canonical CESK at a safepoint\" | \"the parking transitions\"; \"the canonical CESK at an instruction boundary\" |\n| `:264-266` | §7.2.1 resume pc is a static safepoint | historical prefix, §3.7.3 |\n| `:656`, `:663-664`, `:668-674` | \"Only safepoints lift\"; \"a continuation may be lifted only at a safepoint\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:692` | \"`:current-continuation` is not a safepoint: it does not park\" | keep (true) |\n| `:728-734` | linker safepoints (M4) | keep; \"safepoint\" here names the `:module/require` parking transitions |\n| `:762-765` | Quiescence paragraph | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:787-794` | the static safepoint map | keep the map; rename nothing (`:yin.safepoint/*` keys are the published wire names); add \"`def`/`use`/`live` are defined at every pc\" |\n| `:800-805` | conformance \"to each safepoint\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:807-825` | layout memo; \"total on safepoints\"; `:not-at-safepoint` bullet; breakpoint sentence | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:929` | wait entry's safepoint of the same name | keep (names a parking transition) |\n| `:1901-1903` | \"control and K are already absent\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:1912-1913` | \"no engine change\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:1941-1942` | \"not at a liftable safepoint while it holds any of these\" | reword, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2161` | \"runs to its next safepoint\" | amend, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2621-2628`, `:2673` | §7.8 steps 1, 3, 9 | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2690` | outcome rows | redefine; delete `:not-quiescent`, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2839` | \"Resume happens only at a safepoint\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2842` | \"hot loop untouched … over the blocked machine's value\" | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:2931-2942`, `:3100-3130` | harness blocker; 7.11.1 | replace, §3.7.3 |\n| `:3186`, `:3252` | \"the safepoint row\"; \"The safepoint block adds obligations\" | keep (\"row\" names the 7.11.1 row; \"block\" the section) |\n| `yin.vm.semantic.md:356` | \"κ is a captured value, never a safepoint\" | keep |\n| `:657-659` | §4.1 title and first sentence | replace, §3.7.2 |\n| `:680-689` | explicit park; rei