oint` of `canonical-task`; steps 1-2 | replace, §3.7.1 |\n| `:2148-2157` | §8.3 item 12 | replace, §3.7.1 |\n| `:2263-2268` | §9 checks | add, §3.7.1 |\n| `:2409-2425` | second conformance text | historical label, §3.7.1 |\n| `:2443` | cross-engine equality \"at one safepoint\" | §3.7.1 |\n| `:2492`, `:2566-2567` | amendment records | keep (records of earlier edits) |\n| `:2738-2740` | install child \"at a quiescent safepoint except `:blocked`\" | \"a carried child is `:blocked` (wire phase `:parked`) or `:running` (wire phase `:running`)\" |\n| `:2792-2797` | §11 Q6 | answer, §3.7.1 |\n| `yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md:45-49` | stance item 1 | §3.7.4 |\n| `:402-404` | install child \"retains at a safepoint\" | \"retains at a park, halt or fuel boundary\" |\n| `:455-460`, `:466-473` | kind rules; custody table | §3.7.4 |\n| `:797-801` | step 7 contexts | §3.7.4 |\n| `:880` | \"quiescence and safepoint, kind\" | §3.7.4 |\n| `:929` | cross-engine \"to each safepoint\" | §3.7.4 |\n| `:970` | \"safepoint reconstruction obligations\" | \"reconstruction obligations at every boundary\" |\n| `:1027` | §11 | §3.7.4 |\n| `universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:560-579` | §7 eligibility | §3.7.5 |\n| `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:4`, `:227-228`, `:312-314`, `:467`, `:542-544`, `:573-597`, `:655-659` | history of the static safepoint API | historical; entry I-9 points to them, §3.7.7 |\n| `:602-603`, `:622` | \"must check the pc against the static safepoint set\"; \"harness must run each 7.4.1 row\" | historical; I-9 |\n| `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:3742`, `:3759`, `:3777-3798`, `:3827`, `:3882`, `:3900-3901`, `:4145` | 14.1 | §3.7.6 |\n| `yin.vm.linker.md:47`, `:2460`; `code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md:74`, `:780`; `semantic.evaluator.md:1544` | name the concept | keep |\n| `known-gaps.md:27`, `:36` | records | keep; add the new row |\n\n**Code: docstrings, comments, refusals.**\n\n| File:line | Text | Slice and disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rows.cljc:1323`, `:1741` | \"wa