`:137`, `:331-333` | kernel docstring; `vm-hot` entry; `step`/`run` | 6d-a adds `run-fuel`; 6d-b adds the gate guard; docstring names both |\n| `engine.cljc:1458-1491` | `advance-install` \"`running` runs it until it halts or parks\" | 6d-a: budgeted; docstring |\n| `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:1-20`, `:1012-1025` | docstring; \"not at a safepoint\" refusal on a stepped machine | 6d-a: docstring says what it now proves; the refusal row becomes the positive `running-kind` case |\n| `:1057-1066` | `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent` | 6d-a: becomes `a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-carried` (law 1/2 on the F1 and F2 states) |\n| `:1886-1904` | `layout-refusals` \"a kernel stepped to a non-safepoint pc\" | 6e: positive; a hand-built entry outside every body still refuses; a `:push` entry relabels |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
