{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '521,639p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793650000000-architect-6d-plan-v2.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"| `stage_e_scenarios.cljc:184-186` | \"no liftable safepoint, UCF 7.4.1\" | 6d-b: \"a hold, UCF 7.7.4\" |\n\n### 3.9 Slices, order, parallelism, effort\n\nHosts: JVM, Node, Dart for every slice. Verification per `docs/agents/build-n-test.md`: iterate on `bb test:clj`; the three-lane quick tier at landing (`bb test:sub yin.vm`; confirm \"Testing yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\" and every touched namespace in the Node log); the slow tier once at 6d-a landing and once at 6e. Every refusal test asserts zero serves (lift) or zero attaches (lower). Fresh worktree: `mise trust`, `npm ci`. Dart: `loop`/`reduce` over thousands of points (never `for`), frames and windows from `{}`, no floats in the driver. Node: `[:lit nil]` survives `select-keys`; the C2 float tamper is the canary.\n\n**Order and parallelism.**\n\n```\nmodule-pins commit 2 (merging now)  ──►  6d-a (branch srvm-6d-a from master after the merge)\n                                              │\n                                              ├──►  6d-b (srvm-6d-b)   ┐  in parallel; both review-gated\n                                              └──►  6e   (srvm-6e)     ┘  independently; 6d-b merges first\n                                                                            if both are green (the holder\n                                                                            closes the owner's invariant)\n```\n\n- Nothing of 6d runs in parallel with module-pins' merge except writing the 6d-a brief: 6d-a's `rows.cljc` hunks (`lift-task*`, `check-pendings!`, `check-install!`, `restore-task`, `lower-task` opts) are adjacent to or inside commit 2's (`discharge!`/`requires` `:1603-1700`, `check-modules!` `:1883-1963`, `lower-task` `:2273-2350`), and both re-mint `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt`. Branching after the merge re-mints once.\n- 6d-b and 6e are independent of each other and both depend on 6d-a's grammar. The owner's invariant is **not** closed by 6d-a alone (fork-only); 6d-b closes it for the holder.\n- After integration: re-run module-store/free-name discharge and receiver admission at mid-body contexts (module-pins' Q5 host-profile re-discharge meets `run` contexts there).\n\n#### 6d-a: the reference lane\n\n**Change.**\n- `frame.cljc`: S1 (`:96-98`) admits `:run` with its exact key set; C2 (`:117-123`) `(pos? n)` for act and return frames only; C3 (`:124-127`) skips the frame itself for a run; `window-defect` (`:49-61`) takes the wanted set and omits `:window-self` for a run; context `:running` in P1 (`:162-164`); A1-A6, T1 skipped for a run.\n- `rows.cljc`: `row-table` (`:49-69`) `:run`, `:ready`, task slots 17/18; `pending-table` unchanged; `lift-task*` (`:1650-1698`) steps 1-2 and nodes per §3.2; `state-node` (`:1508-1518`) run arm; `validate-frames` (`:1109-1144`) slot 17 in `:running`, slot 18's waits in `:wait`; `check-pendings!` (`:1877-1882`) the kind table; `check-install!` (`:1862`) child kinds by phase; `task-ops` (`:1261`, `:1263-1277`) and `custody-baseline` (`:1297`) kind set and completed-op rule; `protect!` unchanged (slot 13 only); `header-custody` (`:1704-1716`); `restore-task` (`:2253-2268`) running arm and ready restore; `lower-task` docstring/opts; `rows->frame`/`frame->rows` (`:1023-1058`, `:1082`) the run shape; `rows/checkpoint` inspector follows `custody-baseline`.\n- `layout.cljc`: `stack-layouts` (`:118-131`) jump and terminator layouts; `state-prim`/`lower-defect` (`:863-874`, `:916-953`) `:run` arm and slots 17/18 (so a primitive in a running window refuses into the register backend before attach even before 6e).\n- `engine.cljc`: `advance-install` takes a budget (`:1458-1491`); `scheduler-round-fuel` beside `scheduler-round` (`:2315-2326`).\n- `semantic.cljc`: public `run-fuel` (§3.4); no change to `vm-hot`'s loop (the gate guard is 6d-b).\n- Tests: `frame_test`, `rows_test`, `safepoint_harness_test` (stepping driver, laws at every boundary, quick sample, tampers, ready/product cases), `layout_test` (static checks), `semantic_vm_test` (`run-fuel`), `engine_test` (budgeted children).\n- Docs: §3.7.1 (continuation §0.1, §0.2, §1.1-1.3, §2.3, §2.6, §3.2-3.3, §4.3, §5.4, §5.6-5.7, §7.1-7.2, §7.4, §8.3, §8.6, §9, §11, the six sites), §3.7.2, §3.7.3 UCF §7.4.1-7.4.2, §7.9; §3.7.4; §3.7.5; §3.7.7; the known-gaps row.\n\n**Depends on.** Module-pins commit 2 on master.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. `frame-test/run-state-rules`: a `:run` built from `run-fuel` at every boundary of `:worked-example` validates in context `:running`; one tamper per rule: C2 (a float pc → `:pc-kind`; `pc = (count v)` → `:pc-bounds`); a **body-start pc validates**; R1 (a key `≥ k(body)` → `:window-scope`); R2 (one live key removed → `:window-missing`; one dead register added → `:window-extra`); S1 (a `deliver` key, or a `pending` key, on a `run` → `:frame-shape`); P1 (a `run` in context `:wait` → `:pending-presence`; an `act` in context `:running` → `:pending-presence`); an `act` at `p+1` and a `run` at `p+1` with `rd` present both validate and each is refused under the other's kind.\n2. `rows-test/run-and-ready-rows`: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame` identity on every `:run` of item 1; `:run` is five slots (a sixth is `:row-shape` at decode step 2 by raw edit with rehash); a `:wait` whose state cref names a `:run` is `:undecodable` at step 3; a `:ready` whose wait cref names a `:run` row, or whose status is not a keyword, is `:undecodable`; a `:ready` with reason other than `:next`/`:put` is refused at lift `:yin.k/non-portable :ready-reason` with zero serves.\n3. `rows-test/task-product-kinds`: (a) `run-fuel` mid-body → kind `:running`, one `:run`, no waits, no ready; lower restores `:control` at the pc with the trimmed window and runs nothing (zero steps observed through the toy channel); `vm/run` reaches the reference result and trace; relift equals the lift under `canonical-under` in a fresh receiver. (b) **F2 state** (two-callers, one response, sweep, resume): kind `:running` with one `:run` and one `:wait`; law 1 (the remaining waiter completes after the receiver's own response), law 2. (c) **F1 state** (both responses, sweep, resume, `run-fuel 1`): kind `:running` with one `:run` and one `:ready`; law 1 (the queued wake resumes before any new wake, its value delivered once, nothing re-appended: the receiver's call-out stream receives no second request), law 2. (d) the state after `check-wait-set` alone (control nil, waits 1, ready 1): kind `:blocked` with one wait and one ready. (e) a halted activation beside a queued wake (hand-built per §3.1): kind `:blocked`, restored flags `blocked? true`, law 1. (f) negative controls: a `:running` root with two `:run` crefs, with none, with a parked-id, with a result; a `:halted` root with a `:ready`; a `:blocked` root with neither waits nor ready: each `:yin.k/undecodable :kind` (or `:parked-id`) before any attach.\n4. `harness/every-boundary-matches-the-reference` (`^:slow`, `slow/guard`): the stepping driver per §3.6 over the 89 cases (`run-fuel 1`, not `vm/step`); at every boundary with `:control` set: lift, lower into an isolated world, immediate relift (law 2), law 6 with the two window tampers, run to the end (law 1); boundary counts to the park and to the halt pinned per case per host (re-measure once; v1's numbers are the assessment's estimate); the coverage classes of §3.6 each reached; the point count asserted.\n5. `harness/sampled-boundaries-match-the-reference` (quick tier): per bare row (22) five structural boundaries (first body-start reached, the pc after the first primitive `:var`, the pc before the parking instruction, the first `:jump` or `:branch-false` reached, the last `:return` before the halt) plus every boundary of rows 1 and 20; laws 1, 2, 6; about 150 points.\n6. `harness/products-and-refusals`: items 3(b)-(e) through the harness's lift/lower path; a `:run` window holding a cursor-ref, a reified continuation and a nil-valued live register round-trips (rows 14, 16, 22 at the boundary after the capture or the nil load); the `ghost` case lifted at the pc **before** the constant-dead branch refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:obligations #{ghost}}` (Q6 pinned); a held `:observe` still refuses `:reason-mismatch` with zero serves.\n7. `layout-test/static-checks-at-every-pc`: on `layout-corpus` and the matrix's vectors, at every reachable pc: `virt` single-valued over `L(p)`'s physical image; the ordered region form has `|layout(p)| + |uses(p)| = |L(p)|` with duplicates counted, and the set equations of §3.5; **the jump pc of every conditional and every terminator has a layout** (the F5 vectors pinned); sizes asserted per segment.\n8. `engine-test/budgeted-install-children`: a child whose initializer loops for thousands of instructions is stopped by `run-fuel n` at a boundary (phase `:running`, `:control` set), lifted as a `:running` child, lowered under receiver admission, continued to `linked`; a nested initializer; a tick over a tree of `t` tasks executes at most `n × t` instructions (counted through a probe primitive).\n9. `semantic-vm-test/run-fuel`: `run-fuel n` on an active machine equals `n` applications of `vm-hot … 1` (record equality minus telemetry fields); on a blocked machine it is one budgeted round; `maybe-run`'s bridge path is exercised once.\n10. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log shows every touched namespace; the slow tier once at landing on three hosts.\n\n**Days.** 3 implementation + 1.5 review (3 rounds) = 4.5; docs 1 beside it.\n\n#### 6d-b: holder, custody, expiry, recovery\n\n**Change.**\n1. `driver.cljc` `run-cycle` (`:2111-2144`): `:fuel` config key (checked in `check-common!` `:177-207`, positive integer or nil); `(if fuel (sr/run-fuel m0 fuel) (vm/run m0))` under the existing gate and halted guards; **each stage's machine assoc'd into the state before the next tenure check**; `cycle-result` adds `:yin.k/at-boundary true`; `step-active`'s catch ends the run on the state it was handed and records `:yin.k/retained-boundary`; `end-run` keeps the retained machine on the ended state (gated `:ended`, never offered).\n2. `export.cljc`: `kind-of` (`:274-282`) `:running` first; `enter` (`:121-149`) drops `first-refusal` and moves the ready queue into the record (`:ready []` on the machine; `:yin.k/recovery-ready` on fenced restore); `recovery-metadata`/`valid-state?` count ready entries; `abort` unchanged (its conditions are right).\n3. `semantic.cljc` `vm-hot` entry gate guard (§3.3 outcome 4); `run-fuel` inherits it.\n4. `ledger.cljc:277`, `authority/grant.cljc:74-75`: admit `:running`.\n5. Docstrings per §3.8 (driver, compose, export header).\n6. Tests: `driver_test`: a fuelled run preempts a long pure loop at a boundary, the phase stays `:running`, the next tick continues; `hand-off` mints, journals, freezes and offers a `:running` pack; a candidate lowers it (awaiting-grant → grant → `activate`) and reaches the reference result; the five clock-controlled cuts of §3.3 with their assertions; `rehydrate-fenced` byte equality for a running root with a wait and with a ready entry, and the rehydrated machine refuses `vm/step` (\"Gate is closed\"); two competing candidates; stale-source stepping refused; uncertain-offer abort refused; expired-grant admission refused; a halted exclusive root still restores without a grant (F6 regression). `ledger_test`/`grant_test`: a `:running` baseline is offerable; `:halted` is not. `compose_rows_test`: an exclusive world handed off at a boundary completes on the successor; one with a running install child. `stage_e_scenarios`: `[:until \"h1\" :running n] [:hand-off \"h1\"]` with fuel so the hand-off lands mid-body; recovery cut before and after the offer; a tenure-expiry cut between slices asserting the last checkpoint is what recovers.\n7. Docs: §3.7.1 §7.3; §3.7.3 UCF §7.7.4, §7.7.6, §7.8, §7.10, §7.11, §7.11.1, `:2842`; §3.7.6.\n\n**Depends on.** 6d-a. **Days.** 2.5 + 1.5 (3 rounds) = 4.\n\n#### 6e: the cross-engine half\n\n**Change.** `layout.cljc`: `lift-running`/`lower-running` over the kernels' live fields (register `{:pc :registers :frames :continuation :store-of}`, stack `{:pc :stack :frames :continuation :store-of}`); `virt` over a given virtual set (`L(p)` for a run); `register-window` parameterised; nil fill outside `L(p)`; `h->a` relabels `:push`; `slice-window`/`lift-stack` dead-prefix rule (`≥`, prefix dropped, diagnostic); `lower-stack`/`stack-k` unchanged in shape; `safepoint!` run mode (any pc inside a body); `canonical-task` lifts an active kernel as `:running` (with waits and ready as the semantic lift does; backends still refuse installs); `kernel-task` lowers a `:running` machine into a running kernel. No kernel edit. `layout_test`, the harness: laws 4 and 5 at every aligned boundary on the 61 lane cases.\n\n**Acceptance.** Law 4: one root id on three lanes at aligned boundary `i` (stack index after `:push` relabelling), taken and untaken branches both pinned, ordered operand multiplicity pinned; law 5: six ordered pairs at every boundary, each continuing to the reference result, with the **full-payload refusal oracle** of §3.6 (exact refusals and exact successful transfers per case and direction); the `:push` relabelling pinned on one row; **item 6, tail residuals**: either a lane-fragment case with a non-empty ambient layout at a tail call exercises the dead-prefix rule (lift drops, lower omits, law 1 and law 4 hold, the diagnostic reports the count) or the static check `layout(p) = []` at every tail-call pc of the fragment proves none exists and the rule is pinned on a hand-built vector; `layout-refusals` rewritten: a kernel stepped to a non-parking pc lifts on both lanes with zero serves refused; a hand-built entry outside every body refuses `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; the fragment is not widened (rows 7-12 and 17 excluded; row 4 not lowered).\n\n**Depends on.** 6d-a; independent of 6d-b. **Days.** 3.5 + 1.5 (3 rounds) = 5.\n\n#### Effort\n\n| Slice | Implementation days | Review rounds | Days |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6d-a reference lane, grammar, fuel, static layouts | 3 | 3 | 4.5 |\n| 6d-b holder, custody, expiry, recovery | 2.5 | 3 | 4 |\n| 6e cross-engine | 3.5 | 3 | 5 |\n| docs (§3.7, §3.8), split across the three | 1.5 | 1 | 1.5 |\n| **Total** | **10.5** | | **15**, or 10 without 6e |\n\nWhat the review said to keep: targeted counterexamples (F1, F2, F5 states), the all-pc static gates, the quick structural sample, one full three-host run at landing, every custody race and scheduler product. What may be cut during iteration: repetitive broad end-to-end cases. No wall-time is forecast; the slow tier's duration is measured once at 6d-a landing and recorded in the ledger row.\n\nRouting: codex (gpt-6.1-sol, workspace-write, stdin closed), one brief per slice, foreground lanes only, report inside the worktree's `collab/`; Fable reviews at every gate under the Q6 rule; glm/cmd as non-author fallback; commit only on Architect sign-off; never commit `collab/` or `docs/agents/routing-status.md`.\n\n### 3.10 Decisions for the owner (defaults stated so 6d-a can start)\n\n1. **Task slots 17 (`run`) and 18 (`ready`)**, re-minting every pinned root once right after module-pins commit 2. Alternative: a mixed slot 13 `[:refs :wait :run :ready]`, no re-mint, every slot-13 traversal audited for three row kinds. **Recommend 17/18**: it removes F7's misread class by construction, and the re-mint coincides with one already happening.\n2. **Fuel as a holder config key `:fuel`**, default nil (today's behaviour; nothing changes until a composition opts in). **Recommend as stated.**\n3. **No automatic export at the bound in 6d-b**; `hand-off` stays explicit; `:yin.k/at-boundary` is the signal. A later \"arm when remaining tenure < one renewal interval\" policy belongs in `compose`, needs no VM clock. **Recommend as stated.**\n4. **No adoption of a retained boundary**: an ended holder keeps `:yin.k/retained-boundary` for inspection only; recovery is the last durable checkpoint; the documents state the loss. A future ledger rule \"a regrant to the same holder may continue from its retained boundary when the input prefix and next-op-seq agree\" is possible but is new authority and not in 6d. **Recommend as stated.**\n5. **Q6**: keep edge-reachability liveness; pin the pre-branch `ghost` refusal. A \"no\" means a constant-propagation pass in `live-pcs`, a separate slice. **Recommend keep.**\n6. **Completed `:put` wakes are completed operations**: op-id well-formed, excluded from retained writes and `protect!`, never re-appended. **Recommend as stated** (the alternative, counting them as retained, would make the receiver re-append a datom that is already on the stream).\n7. **`:push` relabelled to its successor**, not refused. **Recommend relabel** (no guest semantics run; the stack content is already its successor's).\n8. **Holds stay refusals** (`:observe`, held, unminted cursor, pending close, link cursor not installed), documented as driver seams mid-step that the driver resolves without guest execution; 6d-b verifies each resolves within one cycle and gives any that does not a known-gaps row. **Recommend as stated.**\n\n### 3.11 Risks\n\n1. **A liveness bug surfaces** at a pc no park looked at: law 1 fails there. A finding, not a slice risk; the main reason to run the every-boundary laws.\n2. **The ready carrier meets a wake reason I did not enumerate** (a link wake entering the queue): pinned as `:ready-reason` refusal in 6d-a and reported; widening is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n3. **Re-mint churn**: two re-mints in a week (module-pins, 6d-a). Mitigation: order (§3.9); 6d's own acceptance pins boundary counts and refusal kinds, never root ids.\n4. **Dead-prefix rule untested on a real case** if the fragment has none: 6e item 6 pins it on a hand-built vector; the rule is then a documented check awaiting a natural case.\n5. **Slow-tier time on Dart**: slow tier only; measured once.\n6. **Gate guard cost**: one map read per `run-fuel`/`vm-hot` call; a reviewer confirms it is outside the loop.\n7. **Fuel too small or too large**: a composition knob; default nil.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification honesty\n\n- Every `file:line` above was read in `7c4dff32` today. The review's citations held in every case I checked; where it cited a function by name I read the body.\n- **Run**: one throwaway JVM test namespace reproducing F1, F2 and F5 (transcript excerpts in §1); deleted; `git status` shows only `collab/`. **Not run**: the harness, the slow tier, any Node or Dart lane, any driver or Stage E scenario, any performance probe. Boundary counts and point counts are to be measured once and pinned by 6d-a.\n- **Claims that are checks** (not theorems): `L(p)` sufficient at every boundary; injectivity over `L(p)` at every pc; the ordered stack equation with the jump/terminator layouts at every pc; the dead-prefix rule; the refusal-oracle equality; cross-host boundary-count equality; the per-tree fuel bound.\n- **Not claimed**: that the de Bruijn kernels reconstruct a `run` state today (6e); that the holder can preempt today (`vm/run` at `driver.cljc:2120`); that fuel bounds wall-clock time; that fuel repairs expiry loss (only exporting before the bound does); that a tail call with a non-empty ambient layout exists in the fragment (6e decides); that link wakes never enter the queue (6d-a verifies by reading `poll-links`); that module-pins commit 2's final hunks are exactly those of `origin/srvm-module-pins` at `62ed14fa` (they are what is merging now).\n- **Timestamps**: the brief dates itself 2026-10-17 21:00 +07 and the owner's ruling 2026-10-17; the machine clock at completion reads 2026-10-16 14:40 +07. The header uses the clock; the ruling's date is quoted as the brief gives it.\n\n## 5. Readiness\n\n**Implementation-ready**: 6d-a, as specified in §3.9, under the defaults of §3.10, **the moment module-pins commit 2 is on master**; its brief can be written now from §3.1, §3.2, §3.4, §3.5 (static part), §3.6, §3.9 and the §3.7 text it owns. 6d-b and 6e are specified to the same level and are ready to brief when 6d-a merges; they run in parallel. **Start first**: 6d-a. The owner's invariant is closed for the holder only when 6d-b lands; the plan says so and does not call it closed earlier.\n\nPLAN-V2-READY\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
