{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -8 /tmp/6da-boundaries.log; rg -n '\"'^ERROR|''^FAIL|actual:'\"' /tmp/6da-boundaries.log | head -20; rg -n '\"'^### I-|''^## I-|I-8'\"' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md; sed -n '808,829p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '2730,2748p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md\"","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\n714:**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins, completed in module-pins commit 2).**\n  keeps so that its `lift` is a table lookup. It never travels in a UCF\n  value; a resumer that is a different engine has its own.\n- `lift(engine-state, layout) → canonical frame` and\n  `lower(canonical frame, layout) → engine-state` are total on safepoints and\n  undefined elsewhere. The conformance obligation is `lift ∘ lower = id` on\n  canonical frames, tested against the reference machine's own frames —\n  which is possible precisely because the dynamic half rides in the frame.\n- A request to lift at a pc that is not a safepoint of the segment returns\n  `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` naming the pc. An engine that wants finer\n  interruption granularity must lower the program to a segment that\n  *contains* a `:park` where it wants one: that is a different instruction\n  record, a different address, and a different profile. An engine may not\n  invent safepoints a record does not have, and two engines that disagree\n  about the safepoint set of one address are not both conforming.\n\nSafepoints are datoms, so a query can ask \"where can this program be\nmigrated?\" without running it, and a debugger's breakpoint set is a subset of\nthe safepoint set by construction.\n\n### 7.4.3 The pending wait travels as data — complete, and resumable elsewhere\n\nA parked machine was waiting for something. That something is a resource of\nand rejected the merged-`E` free environment. **Revision 4 (after 6b)\nlists the design choices the merged code made that no ruling covers.**\nEach is stated as the code behaves today; phase-7 closures below leave\nall other questions open.\n\n**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: 7a D2 corrects the plan's equal-baseline variant claim.\nThe baseline includes `:yin.k/root`. Re-emitting an id-counter change\nchanges that root and is `:variant-conflict`. The equal-baseline encoding\nvariant retains the same root with another row order. `emit` sorts rows;\n`decode` still accepts unsorted packs, so one root/one pack is an emission\nproperty, not a reader restriction.\n\n- **Q1, install children, the parked-child scenario.** The engine never\n  retains an install child at a quiescent safepoint except `:blocked` at\n  phase `:parked` (§5.2 B1). The carrier still admits phase `:running`\n  (never engine-reachable at a safepoint) and the lower refuses any\n  child kind but `:blocked`. Should the row table and both checks\n  narrow to the one reachable state (phase `:parked`, child `:blocked`),\n  or does the owner want a reachable parked-child install scenario,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat >> test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc <<'EOF'\n\n\n(defn fuel-drive\n  \\\"Drive to the next guest stop, observing each returned budget boundary.\\\"\n  [m observe]\n  (observe m)\n  (loop [m m n 0]\n    (when (> n 20000) (throw (ex-info \\\"Boundary driver failed to stop\\\" {:steps n})))\n    (let [next (sr/run-fuel m 1)]\n      (observe next)\n      (if (or (:control next) (seq (:ready-queue next)))\n        (recur next (inc n)) next))))\n\n\n(defn check-returned-boundaries\n  [cases]\n  (mapv (fn [[row segment _ build]]\n          (let [points (atom 0)\n                observe (fn [m]\n                          (swap\"'! points inc)\n                          (boundary-round-trip m))\n                expected (reference (build))\n                result (with-redefs [vm/run #(fuel-drive % observe)] (reference (build)))]\n            (is (= expected result) (str row \" \" segment))\n            [row segment @points])) cases))\n\n\n(deftest sampled-returned-boundaries\n  (let [cases (filterv #(contains? #{1 19 20 22} (first %)) (matrix-cases))\n        counts (check-returned-boundaries cases)]\n    (is (= 13 (count counts)))\n    (is (every? pos? (map #(nth % 2) counts)))))\n\n\n(deftest ''^:slow every-returned-boundary\n  (slow/guard \"every-returned-boundary\"\n    (fn []\n      (let [counts (check-returned-boundaries (matrix-cases))]\n        (is (= 89 (count counts)))\n        (println \"6d-a returned-boundary counts JVM:\" (pr-str counts))))))\nEOF\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test > /tmp/6da-boundaries.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
