{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_160","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > /tmp/6da-report.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone,timedelta\nimport re,json,shutil,subprocess\nout=Path('target/6da');out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nfor p in Path('/tmp').glob('6da-*.log'):\n    shutil.copyfile(p,out/p.name.removeprefix('6da-'))\nfor n in ['root-remints.txt','fixture-remints.json','safepoint-inventory.txt']:\n    shutil.copyfile('/tmp/6da-'+n,out/n)\nshutil.copyfile('/tmp/6da-acceptance.clj',out/'acceptance.clj')\nlog=Path('/tmp/6da-acceptance-final.log').read_text()\ncounts=[]\nfor name,passed,failed,errors in re.findall(r'ACCEPTANCE-VAR (\\\\S+) \\\\{:test 1, :pass (\\\\d+), :fail (\\\\d+), :error (\\\\d+)\\\\}',log):\n    counts.append((name,int(passed),int(failed),int(errors)))\nnow=datetime.now(timezone.utc)\nreport=f'''Completed-GMT: {now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT')}\nCompleted-Local: {now.astimezone(timezone(timedelta(hours=7))).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S +07')}\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: 01a14462-7cbe-7bc0-baf0-63a150af5862\n# Slice 6d-a — partial implementation, stopped on design and protected-golden gates\n\nRole: VM Runtime. Branch \"'`srvm-6d-a`, base `b9103797`. Governing specification: plan v2.1, with the retained v2 clauses and glm confirmation. No commit, push, merge, or Fable sign-off is claimed. This report ends BLOCKED; it is not a completion/sign-off report.\n\n## Stops requiring a ruling\n\n1. **Acceptance 9'\"'s set equation fails on the existing corpus.** \"'`layout-test/static-layouts-at-every-pc` retains all assertions and reports four failures: `:resume-operand` and `:tail-operand`, each at PC 1 and PC 2. At PC 1, `L(pc) = #{{}}` while `set(layout) ∪ uses = #{{1}}`; at PC 2 they are `#{{3}}` and `#{{1 3}}`. The ambient operand is already dead before the tail/resume transfer. Adding jump and terminator layouts does not remove it. The requested dead-prefix/running-backend treatment belongs to 6e, and this brief forbids taking that work. I stopped this sub-part rather than removing the fixtures or weakening the equations. An asynchronous scope question remains unanswered: defer those cases'\"' equation gate to 6e, or authorize the required treatment here.\n2. **The boundary driver reaches an unsatisfied setup snapshot.** \"'`safepoint-harness-test/sampled-returned-boundaries`, through `check-returned-boundaries` → `fuel-drive`, observes row 20'\"'s setup batch at its initial PC. \"'`rows/discharge!` refuses `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, discovery `:incomplete`, obligations `#{{s}}`, before the batch defines `s`. I did not change conservative discharge or silently exclude setup. The unanswered scope question is whether the measured row starts after setup, or this slice must admit future store definitions. No complete boundary counts, coverage claim, or per-point law-1 claim is made.\n3. **Protected golden changed.** The grammar changes the transitive ledger fixture. Per the explicit STOP rule, `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/ledger-v2.txt` remains untouched. Read-only rendering gives:\n\n| Protected value | Old | New |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ledger projection digest | `419e3aa652d79cab6921cf7a6c02972bcfe2d3b88ba472bc03ac8f1a935f27d2` | `52f8127f5bcb1643664d665e9e0d3b38bca51039eb66222da4b8fb5824ed1dfb` |\n| BLAKE3 of ledger golden text | `5de18ed0ea8d55ba9d7aa92b6e1eb8bbbb4855d216f6f197af408675c0363e15` | `59a6944da7a7aff3ba351ccd642e371b444f1dcc6be07daeee928b4eec791665` |\n\nThe eight ledger failures in the full quick run are its file/render equality, six frame-byte equalities, and projection equality. The read-only digest evidence is in [focused-final.log](../target/6da/focused-final.log); that helper printed the digests but did not execute tests because its temporary alias omitted the test runner dependency. The subsequent actual focused command is logged separately.\n\n## Implemented parts\n\n- **Frame validation:** distinct closed `:run` shape; PC zero admitted for run only; predecessor continuity skipped only for the run itself; `:pc-body` retained; explicit wanted windows (`saved` for delivery/return, `live` for run); run/ready contexts; completion reason and boolean-try validation through context rather than a fabricated pending. Existing environment and K validation remain.\n- **Rows/carrier:** discriminated `:completion` table with all seven tags, `:run` and `:ready`, task slots 17/18; running/parked/blocked/halted precedence; no ready-queue quiescence refusal; ordered ready lift/restore; independent update bodies under census identities; role-aware numbering/decoded membership traversal; separate completion restoration for retired link/install resources; running restore and fenced recovery-ready retention; run frame bijection.\n- **Custody/inspection:** running kind admitted; completed outcomes excluded from retained writes and protection; `check-op-id-shape!` factored and called directly by slot-18 `check-pendings!`; source/header/grant paths retain the halted exemption. Running-child phase admission is paired with running child kind. The old inspector `bad-kind` fixture exposed acceptance of `:running` without a run row; `task-ops` now also checks run cardinality. Final focused tests verify that regression.\n- **Layouts:** jump-result and terminator layouts; run payload traversal and direct ready delivery-state traversal; ready outcome/refusal and value-bearing descriptor traversal before backend attachment. No dead-prefix or running backend lift was added.\n- **Execution:** `run-fuel` dispatches on control presence, uses one raw budgeted action and at most one bridge step, and returns. Child execution is supplied through the sweep and nested installs. `vm-hot`, `vm/step`, `vm/run`, and `run-fuel` each check the gate once outside the instruction loop; a private raw runner avoids duplicate entry checks. Existing unrestricted `vm/run` bridge behavior remains.\n- **Fixtures/docs:** the existing rows-checkpoint renderer regenerated the allowed fixture. Draft owned amendments cover the continuation carrier/validator/fuel/harness, semantic design, UCF 7.4/7.9, tuples, v2 eligibility, I-9 and known gaps. The document changes are not certified verbatim-complete: the final exhaustive-list/historical-text audit remains unfinished. No 6d-b holder/export/compose/ledger code or docstrings, UCF 7.7/7.10/7.11 hunks, linker-DHT document hunks, or backend jump-lift/dead-prefix implementation were taken.\n\n## Verification actually executed\n\n- `mise trust` completed after the trust-state write required sandbox escalation; `npm ci` passed.\n- The missing lexer was generated with `mise exec -- bb gen:python-antlr`; network access was required to fetch the pinned grammar support files. Generated files are under build; no `src/yang` or `test/yang` files changed.\n- Kondo on all changed source/test files: **0 errors, 0 warnings**. [Log](../target/6da/kondo-final.log). `git diff --check` is clean. Changed Clojure files were formatted with cljstyle.\n- Required focused namespaces, plus rows checkpoint/custody regressions: **205 tests, 7,721 assertions; 4 failures, 1 error**. The failures are only stop 1; the error is stop 2. [Final focused log](../target/6da/focused-final2.log).\n- Whole JVM quick tier, with loopback access: **4,057 tests, 252,249 assertions; 13 failures, 1 error**. [Log](../target/6da/quick-loopback.log). It predates the inspector correction and the final added tests. Its failures divide into four layout equations, eight protected ledger checks, and one inspector `bad-kind` check; its error is the setup discharge. The final focused run verifies the inspector correction. The earlier sandbox-restricted run was terminated after socket denials, then restarted with loopback access; no result is claimed for that interrupted run.\n- Final selected acceptance vars: **{len(counts)} tests, {sum(p+f+e for _,p,f,e in counts)} assertions/outcomes; {sum(f for _,p,f,e in counts)} failures, {sum(e for _,p,f,e in counts)} error**. These include a final full diagnostic-map comparison for link/install errors. [Per-var log](../target/6da/acceptance-final.log), [reproduction script](../target/6da/acceptance.clj). The script exits normally even when `clojure.test` reports failures; the counters, not its exit status, are the evidence.\n- No slow-tier execution, Node/Dart test lane, three-host landing run, or implementation-weakening mutation campaign was performed. A slow boundary test is present but incomplete/unpinned. Fable'\"'s diff confirmation and sign-off remain outstanding.\n\n## Acceptance 1–14 (v2.1 numbering)\n\nCounts below refer to named new tests, can overlap between items, and do not claim the whole item is complete. The exact per-var counters follow this table.\n\n| # | Outcome and assertion evidence | Work still required |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Partial: \"'`run-state-rules` 13/13; existing frame namespace also runs in final focused verification. | Pin worked-example boundary inventory and the complete delivery/run cross-kind cases. |\n| 2 | Partial: run slot/reference grammar 5/5; ready validation/product test 36/36; boolean/update refusals 16/16; site mismatch product 6/6. Lower mutation tests assert zero attaches. | Complete every refusal-slot combination and a weakening mutant for every new rule. |\n| 3 | Partial: running round-trip/fencing 32/32; scheduler products 36/36; halted-with-waits normalization 8/8; halted-ready/site test 6/6. Halted-with-waits is separate from blanket result equality. | Finish the full illegal-kind/result/parked-id matrix. |\n| 4 | Partial: link/install success, try failure and raised failure, after install removal, 48/48; immediate relift and full error-data equality are checked. | Explicit completed link-request producer and active-control-beside-link/install completion cases; once-only effect counters. |\n| 5 | Partial: post-sweep shared identity and ordered actual values are checked in the 36-assertion product test; distinct census/update body case in the 8-assertion portability/update test. | Independent source/receiver continuation equality for the shared-cursor seam and all body-position assertions. |\n| 6 | Partial: completed fork put/history and malformed IDs 20/20; FFI request-append transition 8/8; terminal write 4/4; link/install terminal cases in item 4. | Explicit exclusive completed-history scenario and complete portable terminal-diagnostic normalization. |\n| 7 | BLOCKED by setup discharge. `sampled-returned-boundaries` performs 1,236 passing checks then one error. Slow driver definition exists. | Full isolated receiver execution at each point, law-6 window tampers at each point, pinned per-case park/halt counts and complete coverage classes. No slow counts claimed. |\n| 8 | Partial: queue carried 4/4; products above; pre-branch `ghost` 4/4 with zero serves; existing hold refusal retained. | The specified five structural samples across all 22 bare rows, every-boundary small rows, and the complete cursor/capture/nil inventory. Current quick selection is rows 1/19/20/22 across wrappers plus unwrapped row 20, not the required structural sampler. |\n| 9 | BLOCKED: static checks 712 pass, 4 fail, out of 716. Existing register/layout checks still run. | Scope ruling for dead ambient operands; dynamic ordered region/value/multiplicity checks remain unimplemented. |\n| 10 | Partial: straight-line actual PC instruction counts and nested child budget, 11/11. The former synthetic running child fixture now obtains real running control with `run-fuel` and restores under admission. | Long and nested real initializer lift/lower-to-linked scenarios and full tree accounting. |\n| 11 | Targeted checks pass: pure fuel/gates 16/16; four sequential bridge calls 47/47; diagnostic-only bridge and control-less dispatch 4/4. | Broader instruction-transition instrumentation remains to be completed. |\n| 12 | Targeted checks pass in 16- and 32-assertion tests: four semantic entries, both closed modes, unchanged relift. | Running-plus-ready fenced recovery equality with explicit no-guest/no-scheduler/no-bridge counters. |\n| 13 | Partial: nested ready-only primitive refusal before attach, portable positive, independently emitted update body, 8/8. | Independent state/outcome/descriptor-root oracle tests and complete refusal traversal campaign. |\n| 14 | BLOCKED: kondo clean; final focused and full quick red as above; allowed fixture reminted. | Resolve stops, finish all acceptance work/docs audit/mutants, green JVM quick, and orchestrator'\"'s Node/Dart/three-host slow/landing gates. |\n\n### Exact final selected-test counters\n\n| Test var | Pass | Fail | Error |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'''\nfor name,p,f,e in counts:\n    report+=f'| \"'`{name}` | {p} | {f} | {e} |'\"\\\\n'\nreport+='''\n## Mutant inventory and limits\n\nThese are **invalid-input mutants/constraint probes**, not a completed campaign that edits implementation rules. The separate implementation-weakening campaign requested by the brief is still pending.\n\n- Run PC fractional/out of bounds; run window out of scope/missing/extra; nil live value retained; forbidden deliver/pending; run in wait/ready/captured/parked contexts.\n- Extra run wire slot after raw rehash; wait/ready references naming a run; unknown completion tag; site-incompatible install completion; nonboolean completion try flags.\n- Nonkeyword ready status; unexpected refusal slot; missing update census key; duplicate update key; malformed completed ID map and negative sequence. Lower probes count zero attaches.\n- Missing/duplicate active run; running result/parked-id; running kind removal/cardinality (including the inspector's old bad-kind fixture).\n- Ready-only nested primitive; changed update body under the same C; pre-branch \"'`ghost` with zero serves; closed exporting/ended entry probes; repeated bridge work and diagnostic input; inactive dispatch and nested child instruction budgets.\n\nNo